cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Model Mapper: find which neurons of a language model a concept depends on"
abstract: >-
  Model Mapper maps a concept to the MLP neurons of an open-weights language model that its recall depends on. A
  labeller LLM writes questions whose answer is the concept; the questions the model answers correctly are kept; the
  200 most-attributed neurons are each switched off and the drop in the answer's exact log-odds is measured, next to
  random same-layer neurons, a k curve and attention-head knockouts. It is the method behind the Qwen Neuron Map
  (Qwen3-8B), and its records use the map's format. Tested on Qwen3-0.6B and Qwen3-8B.
